[node name="Body" type="RichTextLabel" parent="CenterContainer/VBoxContainer/ScrollContainer"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(700, 0)
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
bbcode_enabled = true
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 18
theme_override_font_sizes/bold_font_size = 22
text = "[b][font_size=24]Controls[/font_size][/b]
• Move Left / Right — [code]A[/code] / [code]D[/code]
• Jump — [code]Space[/code]
• Attack — [code]Left Mouse Button[/code]
• Interact / Pick Up — [code]E[/code]
• Abilities 1–9 — [code]Q[/code], [code]R[/code], [code]T[/code], [code]G[/code], [code]F[/code], [code]V[/code], [code]Z[/code], [code]X[/code], [code]C[/code]


[b][font_size=24]Advancing[/font_size][/b]
You begin at [b]Sequence 9[/b]. To progress, you must drop your Sequence number one tier at a time, all the way down to [b]Sequence 5[/b].

At the end of each branch you'll find a [b]Sequence Shrine[/b]. Stand near it and press [code]E[/code] to advance. Each shrine requires:
• [b]2 Materials[/b] — found in Material rooms scattered through the world.
• [b]3 Enemy Drops[/b] — the green pickups left behind by defeated enemies. Walk over and press [code]E[/code] to collect them.

If you don't have enough, the shrine won't activate. Clear more rooms and come back.


[b][font_size=24]Sequence Doors[/font_size][/b]
Branches are walled off by [b]Sequence Doors[/b], each labeled with the Sequence number required to pass through it. A door marked \"Seq 7\" stays locked until you advance to Sequence 7 or lower. Once you advance at a shrine, every door you've earned access to opens automatically.


[b][font_size=24]Healing[/font_size][/b]
Some rooms contain a [b]Heal[/b] interactable. Press [code]E[/code] to fully restore your HP. Each heal can only be used once, so save them for when you really need them.


[b][font_size=24]The Goal[/font_size][/b]
The Sequence 5 branch ends in the [b]Boss Room[/b]. Defeat the three-phase boss to win the run.

If you die at any point, the run ends. Good luck."

[node name="BackButton" type="Button" parent="CenterContainer/VBoxContainer"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 48)
text = "Back"
